d #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "206675d2-b06e-5deb-b30d-ae541d334107" :question/math-academy-id "q-20983" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(2)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(2)=0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=2$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=2$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+24x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=6{x}^{2}-24x+24.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12x-24.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =12\\cdot 2-24=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. These points are the solution of the equation ${f}^{′}(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-24x+24 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the only stationary point is $x=2.$\n\nLet's choose auxiliary points from each side of the stationary point and evaluate the first derivative at them. We take the auxiliary points $x=1,3$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =6(1)^{2}-24(1)+24=6>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =6(3)^{2}-24(3)+24=6>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the first derivative does not change the sign at $x=2$, we conclude that $f(x)$ has no relative extrema at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b7e659d-56db-586b-9e30-c199a47f2d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465833} {:answer/id #uuid "41838cf6-58b8-5e7b-91fe-8ddaa9cdf51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41838cf6-58b8-5e7b-91fe-8ddaa9cdf51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465834} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeed986f-a33a-5850-af4c-a59b7f254892" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de977d43-0252-5c01-a917-431cef599417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465835} {:answer/id #uuid "8d16f839-433d-5708-912f-a65fbd85a727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d16f839-433d-5708-912f-a65fbd85a727" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465836} :answer-field/id #uuid "201f9d6e-4534-5596-90d4-245690e6ae7a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b244ad2c-e740-5756-9eb8-97804bc79c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465837} {:answer/id #uuid "d91709c7-2d43-578b-891b-0b8c42602c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465838}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b244ad2c-e740-5756-9eb8-97804bc79c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465837} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee47c52-cc29-52cc-886a-27d07b5a1c28" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1e5b57c-3102-59cd-a153-f7966b8c71f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-21066" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,2)$, $(-1,1)$ and $(3,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(12,6)$\n- **II.** $(4,2)$\n- **III.** $(4,6)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(12,6)$, $(4,2)$ and $(12,6).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105893 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Coordinates of an Image Formed by a Singular Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0c5a18-5e11-5682-aee9-c5b1edaa8279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465839} {:answer/id #uuid "411a4d79-00d3-5b92-ac8a-3ec8a1e3f2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "411a4d79-00d3-5b92-ac8a-3ec8a1e3f2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465840} :answer-field/id #uuid "9421c86b-2a6a-50f6-8512-cf27184b37ad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56f4be8b-4b7c-56a4-9398-01021eea2d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465841} {:answer/id #uuid "1dc9a459-35a8-5a20-9e97-123a79808c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56f4be8b-4b7c-56a4-9398-01021eea2d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465841} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd23d91b-7e49-54fe-974f-8f13e9c8eb9d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367a2d75-1ecd-5ed6-b56c-88c44b0b8e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465843} {:answer/id #uuid "79ca7384-4b46-5ca8-8121-1fb3ddfac730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "367a2d75-1ecd-5ed6-b56c-88c44b0b8e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465843} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcad1d36-8c15-56ba-96ea-8a418c029efc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9622b4aa-6606-5dbb-91d5-63f920f6e03c" :question/math-academy-id "q-21068" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(1,2)$, $(-1,2)$ and $(-1,0)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n- **I.** $(16,8)$\n- **II.** $(8,2)$\n- **III.** $(-4,4)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$ \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(16,8)$, $(8,4)$ and $(-4,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2beee5fa-9bef-5383-a9c4-8f197153726a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465845} {:answer/id #uuid "178776c8-5b13-58a3-af74-43b9a4920dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "178776c8-5b13-58a3-af74-43b9a4920dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465846} :answer-field/id #uuid "63beb250-5e87-52c5-9f14-675220a194f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf2568b9-f9f4-53c4-8e09-04a0f239a570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465847} {:answer/id #uuid "ae14151f-054b-57b3-8e30-192d064b3b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae14151f-054b-57b3-8e30-192d064b3b7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465848} :answer-field/id #uuid "27d88766-cf3f-56c9-aaf4-2204f4fb9d53" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "916be62e-0dc0-5595-8742-ad982de206bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465849} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c663d7-33c4-5849-b63d-28884d3a4cf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "916be62e-0dc0-5595-8742-ad982de206bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465849} :answer-field/id #uuid "800b5f7d-59d0-5331-b789-3c5eb2e6b1bf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48699d28-6189-5c8c-ac56-4e78a856e54a" :question/math-academy-id "q-21500" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15$ on $(0,\\infty ),$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=1$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-3{x}^{5/2}+5{x}^{3/2}+15,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-3\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{3/2}+5\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{3/2}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{1/2}(x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}=-\\frac{45}{4}{x}^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{-1/2},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(1)=-\\frac{45}{4}(1)^{1/2}+\\frac{15}{4}(1)^{-1/2}=-\\frac{15}{2}<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=1$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=1\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1458dc53-ee79-5264-9911-8ed7339cb912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465851} {:answer/id #uuid "776e57cd-230f-5027-88ae-a66b6a45fc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "776e57cd-230f-5027-88ae-a66b6a45fc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465852} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e14f205-4338-574c-984e-57205f445905" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9000b745-54e7-52e5-9d20-5be943c24dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465853} {:answer/id #uuid "b217d6bb-9abe-54de-bf75-219c5f41a1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b217d6bb-9abe-54de-bf75-219c5f41a1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465854} :answer-field/id #uuid "41819972-9642-5ab0-a194-47a7491ed78f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466770} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfc6401a-e444-5077-a023-52e04c085fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465855} {:answer/id #uuid "a157ae35-ee9d-54ba-8019-906609e47187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfc6401a-e444-5077-a023-52e04c085fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465855} :answer-field/id #uuid "8678397e-2f2b-55b8-a327-5e1713aee4b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b9fc172-9b76-5d55-bed8-430ab7579f16" :question/math-academy-id "q-21504" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+36x-48,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=3$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(3)<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=3$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=3$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+36x-48,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-12x+36,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+36 & =0 \\\\ -12(x-3) & =0 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have a critical point at $x=3.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-12,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=3$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(3)=-12<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=3,$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=3$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(3)<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=3\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87928282-25c7-5242-b6a9-a326a31e5510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465857} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb156f2-8c5a-5428-9cb7-abb0cfc8d04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb156f2-8c5a-5428-9cb7-abb0cfc8d04a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465858} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fc704cc-93de-5236-8fdd-91b84b0721dd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb8061e-5904-53cd-ab23-286784a69b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465859} {:answer/id #uuid "8111909c-3b03-5a88-8ce3-703789b528f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bb8061e-5904-53cd-ab23-286784a69b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465859} :answer-field/id #uuid "210a5297-8bb8-5ab6-9045-5bb795d6bde0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd5a3b95-e006-528c-a0c5-8a57536f5280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465861} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebf830d-3243-5b5b-a136-110ffb2af812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ebf830d-3243-5b5b-a136-110ffb2af812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465862} :answer-field/id #uuid "62de44fc-65f2-5ef9-af42-631eb8d0a7a6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2b37341-4b83-58cd-8078-617f2c8f3e30" :question/math-academy-id "q-22011" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(-6)<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-6$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=-6$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ -{x}^{2}(x+6)(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =-6,0,6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=-6,0,6.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=-6.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=72x-4{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=-6$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-6)=432>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=-6,$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=-6$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-6)<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=-6\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee50943-da0c-5eb5-b2f8-b23f8c2e2962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465863} {:answer/id #uuid "da99fa0d-321e-5f45-9408-87319e559341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da99fa0d-321e-5f45-9408-87319e559341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465864} :answer-field/id #uuid "130f3f1b-18e0-559e-a756-d5a532252295" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3430b47f-98c6-5d2f-942f-81215b4cbc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465865} {:answer/id #uuid "c64e37d6-0a0b-5b63-b0ff-3c87bbe1d80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3430b47f-98c6-5d2f-942f-81215b4cbc00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465865} :answer-field/id #uuid "221e1b3f-0f02-5f36-ab41-cab13c8646e8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e344f84-a25f-5a7a-8f4d-4e58384a648d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465867} {:answer/id #uuid "47bf9edb-8d51-58f7-b466-69861f4dc405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47bf9edb-8d51-58f7-b466-69861f4dc405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465868} :answer-field/id #uuid "5656ba5f-9174-562a-a795-3a1018968dad" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "247bae04-64ae-5dcd-80c8-d60760babf45" :question/math-academy-id "q-22015" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=3{x}^{5}-10{x}^{3}+9,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\sqrt{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=3{x}^{5}-10{x}^{3}+9,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=15{x}^{4}-30{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}^{4}-30{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 15{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2) & =0 \\\\ 15{x}^{2}(x+\\sqrt{2})(x-\\sqrt{2}) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{2},0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm \\sqrt{2},0.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=60{x}^{3}-60x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})=60(\\sqrt{2})^{3}-60\\sqrt{2}=60\\sqrt{2}>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=\\sqrt{2},$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{2}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{2})>0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=\\sqrt{2}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbee870b-4a67-5ccb-b274-45fac627be6e" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a Given Critical Point Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b64840-cdbe-51af-ae5f-3a1ebf8b1eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465869} {:answer/id #uuid "539318a7-8cb6-5daa-ac08-572b27b2eefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b64840-cdbe-51af-ae5f-3a1ebf8b1eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465869} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6979f09-27c3-5d99-9841-fa7bd5afc99f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a094ef95-0842-544f-84d8-c97acfe7948f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465871} {:answer/id #uuid "0c337dc8-1ff2-57f1-8269-8ae05c9eabc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a094ef95-0842-544f-84d8-c97acfe7948f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465871} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cb6da3-66a0-5d6d-bb97-d9e8dc4ae9a3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9cf2d5-1469-5f57-84ae-a729db035dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465873} {:answer/id #uuid "6e07279a-94d0-531f-b4bb-b71ad949ca26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b9cf2d5-1469-5f57-84ae-a729db035dda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465873} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e397c8-64d1-536f-bccc-4b61bf84365f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cfe05852-ce59-5bf2-a32a-e36a882c576e" :question/math-academy-id "q-22016" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(1)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(1)<0$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We're given that $x=1$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+36x+12,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=36{x}^{2}+24x-60.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1) & =36(1)^{2}+24(1)-60=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is zero, we conclude that the test is inconclusive, we need to use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's  find other stationary points. Solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-60x+36 & =0 \\\\ 12({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-5x+3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)({x}^{2}+2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 12(x-1)(x-1)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have two stationary points, $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ Next, to determine whether these points are local maxima or minima, we use the first derivative test.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=-4,0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-4) & =12(-4-1)^{2}(-4+3)=-300<0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =12(0-1)^{2}(0+3)=36>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =12(2-1)^{2}(2+3)=60>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $-3$ | $(-3,1)$ | $1$ | $(1,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $-4$ |  | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $↘$ | min | $↗$ |  | $↗$ |\n\nAt $x=1,$  the first derivative does not change the sign. Therefore, $x=1$ is neither a local minimum nor a local maximum.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a8b8711-c268-57c6-a577-dec262c6aebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465875} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1a90bb-55e6-5cba-99f5-a105b2e2a0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd1a90bb-55e6-5cba-99f5-a105b2e2a0e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465876} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ac8980-665e-5f33-8864-5cc859b00f77" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc1b4480-28b8-589d-b1aa-b548596cf756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465877} {:answer/id #uuid "660da3fb-825b-5184-8c0f-537971146519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc1b4480-28b8-589d-b1aa-b548596cf756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465877} :answer-field/id #uuid "d989fce0-4941-56f0-a595-345603843901" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466782} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0834cb3-be65-5030-9b56-93f46726966c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465879} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9222fb-5bff-59e0-aaa2-f93b404965f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e9222fb-5bff-59e0-aaa2-f93b404965f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465880} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f4c2d3-efda-58b7-964d-c56196f0f817" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e347cb6-d962-5b7a-b93a-2a8ccafaafbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-22080" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)={x}^{5}-5{x}^{3}+15,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\sqrt{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{5}-5{x}^{3}+15,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{4}-15{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{4}-15{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-3) & =0 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}(x+\\sqrt{3})(x-\\sqrt{3}) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3},0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3},0.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=20{x}^{3}-30x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})=20(\\sqrt{3})^{3}-30\\sqrt{3}=30\\sqrt{3}>0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is positive at $x=\\sqrt{3},$ so this critical point is a relative *minimum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\sqrt{3}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\sqrt{3})<0\\,\\times $\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *minimum* at $x=\\sqrt{3}\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0273afcf-1982-5569-8348-f10a8e77aad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465881} {:answer/id #uuid "1526315c-74f6-5bb1-a15f-52ce2cf483f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465882}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1526315c-74f6-5bb1-a15f-52ce2cf483f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465882} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a11075d-7e91-53e3-8287-8ac5fd97acb2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c496d87e-e47e-5f9d-8298-d6c0c32cca85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465883} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5f781a-5bc0-57ae-80e8-0675eb804587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b5f781a-5bc0-57ae-80e8-0675eb804587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465884} :answer-field/id #uuid "d88e12bf-9078-5424-8848-e2cb1e920461" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3910ecb-9299-5ff4-844f-6a07a3aa9e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465885} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbca59f-a430-5c3d-8b2e-b5eb1ff6889e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3910ecb-9299-5ff4-844f-6a07a3aa9e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465885} :answer-field/id #uuid "5770f9b6-676c-5c90-9086-6fea3b63ca67" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "527ec064-c6b0-5d4a-ac97-7dea39646f9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-22495" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)$\n- **II.** ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})<0$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We need to identify whether $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point. If it is, we then need to classify it using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & =0 \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi , \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$ We're interested in the critical point $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at this critical point. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2<0.\n$$\n\nThe second derivative is negative at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ so this critical point is a relative *maximum*. \n\nTherefore, comparing our results with the given statements, we conclude that:\n\n- $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a critical point of $f(x)\\,✓$\n\n- ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})<0\\,✓$\n\n- $f(x)$ has a relative *maximum* at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 