 #uuid "3910cc85-5508-5c6f-b6b0-d5041c8c1376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77aecb7e-3a12-52e2-a0a0-4f675ac7f167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465891} :answer-field/id #uuid "57297f62-17f1-58b7-8a9b-a5c727ad1f39" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c687bf7b-334e-54f3-b20c-cd4bb1895323" :question/math-academy-id "q-22826" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x}$ defined on $x\\in (0,\\infty ).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is concave up on $(0,1)$\n- **II.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,1)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is concave down on $(1,\\infty )$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & >0 \\\\ 2 & >\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {x}^{3} & >1 \\\\ x & >1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that $x>0.$\n\nHence, ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ when $x>1.$ So the graph is concave up on the interval $(1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality $2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}<0,$ which has the solution $(0,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059683 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bba0ad98-6940-502a-873c-8a589a03a499" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Coterminal Angles in Degrees"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "438e4ae1-dec4-541f-bc71-9f29cc1eaab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465893} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9ced1e-ad94-566f-aeda-fe4c34436c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a9ced1e-ad94-566f-aeda-fe4c34436c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465894} :answer-field/id #uuid "daad3acd-b8bf-5e86-910c-d0a63a90988e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f55be858-1473-5d1c-8a52-ac1046a9bb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465895} {:answer/id #uuid "7ea7713b-f938-50c1-aeb3-3e1053fc94d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f55be858-1473-5d1c-8a52-ac1046a9bb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465895} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c75c20-6d08-50bd-a57a-7fc6e93f4c49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed1fbb42-76aa-5dee-a67f-6420ccdefab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465897} {:answer/id #uuid "0244befe-f2f7-56a7-b536-ba23abf3af78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0244befe-f2f7-56a7-b536-ba23abf3af78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465898} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e17448c-1e24-55f5-8b2e-03cef8ac95c2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca248134-22cf-5031-924c-1fcc047804dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-22979" :question/problem "Which of the following angles are coterminal with $\\theta =-{95}^{∘}?$\n- **I.** ${625}^{∘}$\n- **II.** ${160}^{∘}$\n- **III.** $-{455}^{∘}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{95}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={265}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={625}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{∘}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{95}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{95}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{455}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{∘}$ and $-{455}^{∘}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{∘}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c29fd2a-ae48-52ee-ba67-7067dea380f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465899} {:answer/id #uuid "14c90ded-4dbd-5cc9-b578-8bbcf18e2466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c29fd2a-ae48-52ee-ba67-7067dea380f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465899} :answer-field/id #uuid "06a90856-9f38-5923-8454-f545e75c55a3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c64831ae-fe38-5483-9592-34c5ba078eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465901} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9bc399-e38e-51c9-a24b-0515e5e03aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9bc399-e38e-51c9-a24b-0515e5e03aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465902} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d4d7c55-71d2-50d5-95fe-51e81764dd1c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83cdc54b-214f-5986-8b82-254b42883bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465903} {:answer/id #uuid "acac67e3-2f8e-55cd-b42c-649006d58792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83cdc54b-214f-5986-8b82-254b42883bae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465903} :answer-field/id #uuid "954c2c17-de3e-55b9-acbc-5eb1abb3d144" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466795} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468616b9-692e-5d47-8126-953037fcb574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465905} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3be01e-97a7-508b-b3c9-0ecc4baeb375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3be01e-97a7-508b-b3c9-0ecc4baeb375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465906} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55e8f74-90ed-54c3-aa6c-dbaf15781e10" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54523433-2b3d-5350-9453-344ec229fc6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-2469" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3},$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(0)<0$\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$\n- **III.** ${f}^{″}(1)>0$\n- **IV.** $x=1$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=6{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=12x-12{x}^{2},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12x-12{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12x(1-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,1.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=12-24x,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =12>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(1) & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false while statement IV is true. The second derivative is negative at $x=1,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae256269-0bec-5d57-ac4a-eb0b07926f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Critical Points and Then Classifying Them Using the Second Derivative Test"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0816a5ca-d233-5de3-b278-dbb902670115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465907} {:answer/id #uuid "f96b1b20-d897-5062-93f6-064bcde23260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f96b1b20-d897-5062-93f6-064bcde23260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465908} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b45853-6985-5b1c-a81d-b66dab8d14e0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99387c6c-3ddf-5e6c-999e-d41fdd79f070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465909} {:answer/id #uuid "1d219022-9306-536f-949c-6d874ce26dbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99387c6c-3ddf-5e6c-999e-d41fdd79f070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465909} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccc10a60-f3da-5766-9a59-91d8841ae5e6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466798} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039db766-6a2b-5ff0-9a62-f0e43addb0ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465911} {:answer/id #uuid "39662058-7b0d-5dc9-907a-8c4194cce15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39662058-7b0d-5dc9-907a-8c4194cce15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465912} :answer-field/id #uuid "878ea395-503e-5466-87e1-15fafb7cda6c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0baea45a-e521-55e5-a85e-0c96f76c085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465913} {:answer/id #uuid "eef39c75-0496-5cd9-98db-a11876ef340b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0baea45a-e521-55e5-a85e-0c96f76c085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465913} :answer-field/id #uuid "beccd9e8-da77-5e9d-bc60-9f35d6fbabba" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19694b62-f531-5e43-9d81-ba1b9a788be0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2471" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-10,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$\n- **III.** ${f}^{″}(-2)<0$\n- **IV.** $x=-2$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-10,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=15{x}^{2}+30x,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}^{2}+30x & =0 \\\\ 15x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,-2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=30x+30,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =30>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(-2) & =-30<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I is true while statement II is false. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statements III is true while statement IV is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=-2,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceaf758c-a8dd-5a9a-adee-637fa878f318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465915} {:answer/id #uuid "36706676-91f8-50e4-adfb-60ef265d6f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36706676-91f8-50e4-adfb-60ef265d6f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465916} :answer-field/id #uuid "d82bf7ae-578c-5f2b-9416-c4e0327e5258" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f2539d-95b7-53fa-a714-8f58f9a9072d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465917} {:answer/id #uuid "35643f7e-51f3-58ac-8d43-310fefbcf937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35643f7e-51f3-58ac-8d43-310fefbcf937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465918} :answer-field/id #uuid "21d81d7d-ae51-58cc-855e-0239b4ddc4ba" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466802} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa265853-ac3f-54ad-b2e1-197486cd24ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465919} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f6d4ed-c8d7-54de-b410-4c092cb9100b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa265853-ac3f-54ad-b2e1-197486cd24ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465919} :answer-field/id #uuid "369d61de-0362-5726-9043-d7210b37adca" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c70458e-a9c0-5f53-8bd6-90f09521b402" :question/math-academy-id "q-253144" :question/problem "Which of the following linear recurrence relations are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}+5{a}_{n-2}$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}={b}_{n-1}+3{b}_{n-2}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}=4{c}_{n-1}+7n$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A linear recurrence relation (with constant coefficients) is **homogeneous** if the forcing function is zero. \n\nIn other words, the linear recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={s}_{1}{a}_{n-1}+{s}_{2}{a}_{n-2}+…+{s}_{k}{a}_{n-k}+g(n),\n$$\n\nis homogeneous if $g(n)=0$ for all $n,$ and ${s}_{i}$ is constant for each $i.$\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- ${a}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${a}_{n-1}$ and ${a}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${b}_{n}$ is homogeneous. The terms of the expression each contain a preceding term, ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}.$\n\n- ${c}_{n}$ is not homogeneous. The term $7n$ of the expression doesn't contain preceding terms of the relation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a42de4ff-e6ae-5cd0-a779-289253a7aa66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465921} {:answer/id #uuid "2e189d6c-8ef7-539f-b37f-87d967920ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a42de4ff-e6ae-5cd0-a779-289253a7aa66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465921} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a0f5a4-4ed4-51c8-be72-bc1c74b87ed7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466804} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da65221a-be97-5688-8bd6-0d038b753c89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465923} {:answer/id #uuid "49f88e20-d91f-5914-9c9d-d823f5133e73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da65221a-be97-5688-8bd6-0d038b753c89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465923} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcadfd18-6479-5741-a737-46067ac802f1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100989ed-9df9-5bed-8d9f-5d7deedc7db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465925} {:answer/id #uuid "d293d52d-2035-55a0-bb5f-6f14c2e9051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d293d52d-2035-55a0-bb5f-6f14c2e9051f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465926} :answer-field/id #uuid "81bda147-d05b-535a-b0e7-50b958de0862" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e47f465-4e25-5a70-adfe-d172f722b8f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-253467" :question/problem "Which of the following recurrence relations are first-order?\n- **I.** ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{a}_{n-2}}{2}+3$\n- **II.** ${b}_{n}=2{b}_{n-1}-{b}_{n-2}$\n- **III.** ${c}_{n}={c}_{n-1}+\\frac{1}{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-2}$ in the relation is $2.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $2.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129287 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4ade459-9aba-5520-95d3-69ef3fd62d9d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Recurrence Relations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5da79ef1-96cb-5b4e-9a6b-18070aae8aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465927} {:answer/id #uuid "398214ec-746e-